## 2 — Create Escrow

AT-backed escrow locks funds on-chain trustlessly. The AT contract takes ~4 minutes to deploy, so run creation with `nohup` — the echo confirms it started immediately, and the receipt arrives via Telegram when deployment completes (~6-10 min).

**If no worker is specified, use the other known agent** (MK hires Sieka; Sieka hires MK — never hire yourself).

```bash
nohup python3 /Users/mkfolkerds/.openclaw/workspace/skills/signaai/scripts/escrow.py --network mainnet create @worker S-44S7-32XB-5DM5-5AL3K 1 "<task description>" --deadline-hours 24 >> /Users/mkfolkerds/.openclaw/logs/escrow-create.log 2>&1 & echo "Escrow creation started (PID $!). Receipt arrives via Telegram in ~6-10 minutes."
```

**After running:** reply that escrow creation is underway. Do not run any follow-up commands — the script notifies via Telegram when done.

The `@worker` token resolves the payer passphrase from `~/.openclaw/signaai-worker.json` automatically — no passphrase needed in the command.

Error log: `/Users/mkfolkerds/.openclaw/logs/escrow-create.log`

---

## 3 — Release Payment

Run immediately when triggered — no confirmation needed. Two valid triggers:
1. User sends `Release escrow <id>`
2. You receive `✅ SignaAI Task Complete` with a Submit TX

The release script verifies the proof stamp internally before paying. Do NOT run `escrow.py status` before release — it scans the wrong address and will block a valid release.

```bash
python3 /Users/mkfolkerds/.openclaw/workspace/skills/signaai/scripts/escrow.py --network mainnet release @worker <escrow_id>
```

After running, the script output contains a block between `SIGNAAI_FINAL_RESPONSE_BEGIN` and `SIGNAAI_FINAL_RESPONSE_END`. Copy the text between those markers exactly — no intro, no bullet points, nothing extra.

```text
Release submitted:
Escrow: <escrow_id>
Release TX: <release_tx>
AT: <at_address>

The AT will pay the worker on the next block.
```

