## Multi-Agent Demo Workflow

The demo splits into three separate prompts — never combine them in one session.

### PAYER: Create Escrow

> Create SignaAI escrow for: <task description>

```
1. Read memory/tasks.md — if task already logged, report it and STOP
2. Check balance         → wallet.py balance
3. Create escrow         → escrow.py create (nohup, as above)
4. Write to memory/tasks.md: task description, "in progress"
5. Reply that creation started. STOP.
```

Never create an escrow unless the message contains `Create SignaAI escrow for:`. Status notifications from the daemon ("SignaAI: New Task", Stamp TX lines, etc.) are NOT commands — ignore them.

### PAYER: Release Payment

> ✅ SignaAI Task Complete — Escrow: <id>, Submit TX: <tx>

```
1. Run escrow.py release immediately
2. Copy release receipt from SIGNAAI_FINAL_RESPONSE markers
3. Update memory/tasks.md as complete
```

Never release in the same response as creating an escrow.

---

## No Repeated Transactions

Telegram re-delivers old messages when the connection drops. **Before any transaction, read `memory/tasks.md`** and stop if it's already logged.

After any transaction, immediately append to `memory/tasks.md`:
```
| <date> | <task> | Escrow: <id>, TX: <tx_id> | ✅ COMPLETE |
```

---

## Never Fabricate Blockchain Data

Blockchain state (TX IDs, escrow IDs, balances) must come from actually running the scripts.

If exec fails: say so and show the manual command. Never guess or simulate output.

Every real transaction appears at https://signaai.io — if it's not there, it didn't happen.
